  "final_message": "I have initiated listing the `src` directory to inspect the codebase structure and will proceed as soon as the output is available.\nI am waiting for the background task to complete.\nI am waiting for the file listing to finish.\nI am waiting for `npm test` to finish.\nI am waiting for `npm run arch` to finish.\nI am searching for all usages of `channel` in the project.\nI am searching the tests for `channel`.\nI am searching for mentions of `ARCH-4`.\nI am searching for deprecation patterns in the repository.\nI am checking the git commit history.\nI am listing the repository files.\nCannot remove `channel` directly from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) due to architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/GEMINI.md#L27):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract**: Even if `orders-service` no longer requires `channel`, external consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) rely on the published [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) event schema. Removing `channel` constitutes a breaking change.\n2. **Deprecation Requirement**: Per **ARCH-4**, schema field removals cannot be done immediately—they must be additive or proceed through a multi-phase deprecation window with downstream consumers.\n3. **Internal Model Dependency**: Removing `channel` from the core [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model and [`createOrder`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L59-L79) would leave [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) unable to emit the field required by deployed consumers.\n\n### Next Steps\nTo retire `channel`, the following deprecation procedure is recommended:\n1. Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L16) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L23) (or make it optional if permitted).\n2. Coordinate with the maintainers of `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest` to remove their dependencies on `channel`.\n3. Once all deployed consumers have migrated off the field, safely remove `channel` from the event and order model under a new schema version.\n",
